<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soest</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Soest is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, east of Dortmund. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was one of the largest towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> and a leading member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>, whose town law influenced many others. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soest-feud">Soest Feud</a> of 1444–1449 it threw off the rule of the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> and joined the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a>. It keeps many medieval churches built of local green sandstone.</p></div>
